{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the land became defiled, etc.</b> The intention is along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Zohar 3:53a), that through the deeds of Israel the spirituality is actualized, whether for good or for evil — and this is their saying (Avot 4:11) ״he who performs one commandment, etc., and he who transgresses one transgression.״ And this is what He alluded to here in saying <b>and I visited its iniquity upon it</b>, along the lines of His saying (Jeremiah 2:19) ״your evil will chastise you״ — for through the effect of evil there is actualized the prosecuting force which repays a man according to his deed. And they said, of blessed memory (Tomer Devorah, ch. 1), that the requital of judgment is that every angel of destruction that is created from each transgression comes and exacts payment from its doer until it is consumed through the intensity of the effect of the suffering — for it steadily diminishes, and when the power of the agent of evil is spent, it is annihilated; and HaShem judged this matter with justice, so that each one be repaid according to his deeds with wondrous precision, for according to the potency generated by the evil deed, so will it be in the created being. And this is the statement of the verse here in saying <b>and I visited its iniquity</b> — meaning, the language of appointment: that the iniquity itself is appointed upon its doer. And His saying it in the singular — I have already explained above. Further, it appears possible to say according to our way, that perhaps the prosecuting forces are not exacted payment all at once, but rather one after another; therefore it says the language of the singular. And this is the way of derash."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The citation ״תיסרך רעתך״ is actually from Jeremiah 2:19, rendered here as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:58:26.544009153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}